# Audit artifacts
_audit/

# Generated, non-source-of-truth artifacts. Each is regenerated on demand
# by a script and validated by its gate; tracking them only inflated the
# pack store and produced merge noise. (Vendored third-party assets such
# as axe-core stay committed -- vendoring is deliberate for reproducible,
# offline builds; only OUR generated output is untracked here.)
#   - .test_durations.integration  pytest-split shard timings for the
#                             integration arm. Untracked because that arm's
#                             27.5-minute budget swallows an unbalanced split;
#                             the unit arm's does not, so ITS timings are
#                             tracked (see below).
#   - data/codebase_map.json  regenerated + structure-validated by
#                             scripts/check_feature_index_freshness.py
.test_durations.integration
data/codebase_map.json

# .test_durations.unit is deliberately TRACKED. Absent, pytest-split falls
# back to partitioning by test COUNT, which measured 141s-322s across four
# equally-sized unit shards and put shard 1 (which collects the
# app-construction tests) over the 300s session cap. Refresh it on demand
# with `make test-durations RUN_ID=<ci-run>`; it is not auto-committed,
# because a weekly rewrite of a 8.5k-entry file is the merge noise that
# retired the previous refresh workflow.

# Benchmark scorecards emitted by `make benchmark`
.benchmark/

# Inner-loop A/B recording scratch: the per-cell workspaces the loops write
# into, the host's throwaway database, and the operator's own recording config
# and credential. Untracked because `capture_provenance` stamps
# `git status --porcelain` into every scoreboard, so a recorder writing here
# would mark its own artifact dirty on a clean checkout and retire the staleness
# signal the scoreboard leans on. The scoreboard itself is committed, under
# evals/loop_ab/scoreboard/.
.loop-ab/

# Per-repo Claude/OpenCode runtime state (not config). Currently:
# - last-push.json (used by scripts/check_push_throttle.sh)
.claude/state/

